---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import SystemConcept from '../components/SystemConcept.astro';
const sections = ['Knowledge Engineering Process', 'Knowledge Acquisition', 'Knowledge Representation', 'Reasoning Process', 'Example Decision Scenario', 'Prototype Development', 'Project Timeline'];
const id = (title: string) => title.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ', '-');
const weeks = [['Week 1', 'Scope & questions', 'Define the decision problem and candidate scenarios.'], ['Week 2', 'Knowledge acquisition', 'Identify sources and record relevant domain concepts.'], ['Week 3', 'Knowledge representation', 'Choose a representation and draft decision logic.'], ['Week 4', 'Prototype', 'Connect contextual inputs, reasoning and explanations.'], ['Week 5', 'Evaluation', 'Review behaviour against agreed scenarios and constraints.'], ['Week 6', 'Reflection & reporting', 'Document findings, limitations and next steps.']];
---
<SiteLayout title="Knowledge Engineering" description="The proposed knowledge acquisition, representation and reasoning process behind the Demand Response Advisor.">
<Hero eyebrow="Knowledge Engineering / Method" title="From domain knowledge to an explained decision." description="A transparent account of how knowledge will be acquired, structured and used in the proposed advisory system." />
<section class="container section"><SystemConcept /></section>
<div class="soft"><div class="container section editorial"><aside class="contents" aria-label="On this page"><p>On this page</p>{sections.map(title => <a href={'#' + id(title)}>{title}</a>)}</aside><div>
<section id="knowledge-engineering-process" class="document-section"><h2>Knowledge Engineering Process</h2><p>The proposed process starts by defining a decision problem, then acquiring domain knowledge, choosing a representation, developing reasoning and reviewing recommendations against agreed scenarios.</p><p>The process is intended to be iterative: gaps or conflicting knowledge should lead to revisions in both the knowledge base and the prototype. The detailed method is to be defined.</p></section>
<section id="knowledge-acquisition" class="document-section"><h2>Knowledge Acquisition</h2><p>Candidate knowledge areas include demand response concepts, consumer flexibility, price signals, grid conditions and user constraints. Relevant literature, domain documentation and possible expert knowledge may inform this stage.</p><div class="callout"><h3>To be defined</h3><p>Sources, datasets, expert involvement and acquisition activities have not been established. Content will be added during the project; no interviews or collected evidence are claimed here.</p></div></section>
<section id="knowledge-representation" class="document-section"><h2>Knowledge Representation</h2><p>The knowledge base is expected to capture domain concepts, relationships, constraints and decision logic. Rules are a candidate representation, but the final approach has not been selected.</p><ul><li>Domain vocabulary and conceptual model: to be defined.</li><li>Rule format, source provenance and versioning: to be defined.</li><li>Handling of incomplete or conflicting knowledge: to be defined.</li></ul></section>
<section id="reasoning-process" class="document-section"><h2>Reasoning Process</h2><p>The intended reasoning process will interpret available inputs, check relevant constraints and identify a feasible recommendation. An explanation should connect the suggested action to the context and knowledge used.</p><p>Inference strategy, conflict resolution and behaviour when information is missing remain under development. The site does not run an inference engine.</p></section>
<section id="example-decision-scenario" class="document-section"><h2>Example Decision Scenario</h2><div class="callout"><span class="badge">Illustrative only ? Not implemented</span><h3 style="margin-top:1rem">A flexible task during a high-price period</h3><p><strong>Context:</strong> A consumer has a task that can be delayed within a permitted time window, and a lower-price period may be available later.</p><p><strong>Reasoning to explore:</strong> Check whether delaying the task respects its deadline, user preferences and any relevant constraints.</p><p><strong>Possible recommendation:</strong> Suggest a later start only if the required conditions are satisfied, and explain the reason for the suggestion.</p><p>This is a discussion scenario, not a validated rule or evidence of savings. Actual inputs, thresholds and decision logic are to be defined.</p></div></section>
<section id="prototype-development" class="document-section"><h2>Prototype Development</h2><p>The planned prototype will connect selected inputs to a knowledge base and reasoning component, then display a recommendation and explanation. Tools, interfaces, datasets and evaluation criteria are to be defined.</p><p>Implementation notes and evidence will be published in the development blog as they become available.</p></section>
<section id="project-timeline" class="document-section"><h2>Project Timeline</h2><p>A proposed six-week structure for development and blog updates. This is a planning outline, not a record of completed work. Dates and responsibilities are to be confirmed.</p><ol class="timeline">{weeks.map(([week, title, description]) => <li><strong>{week}</strong><div><strong>{title}</strong><span>{description}</span><span>Planned ? Dates to be defined</span></div></li>)}</ol></section>
</div></div></div></SiteLayout>
